+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. The library can apply an RFC 6902 JSON Patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in scope: unchanged parts of the document are never mentioned, objects and arrays are compared recursively, and a small change deep in the document yields a small, deep operation.
+- Array item insertions and removals yield only `add`/`remove` of that item; item moves yield a `move` (not rewrites of the items in between).
+- Neither input is mutated, and the patch shares no objects or arrays with the inputs.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-creation`: producing a minimal RFC 6902 JSON Patch from two JSON document versions.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/json-patch-creation.ts`, new export in `src/index.ts`, new tests, README entry.
+- No new dependencies; `applyPatch` is unchanged.
